# Feature Test Case IDs

Every `Scenario` and `Scenario Outline` in ICM `.feature` files must have a unique test case ID tag.

## Format

`@TEST-{NNN}-{Module}-{Area}` — `TEST` prefix, three-digit zero-padded sequence, then module and area slug.

| Feature area | Area tag (kebab) | Test case ID example |
|---|---|---|
| Product create page | `@product-create-page` | `@TEST-001-Product-Create-Page` |
| Product edit page | `@product-edit-page` | `@TEST-001-Product-Edit-Page` |
| Commission structure | `@commission-structure` | `@TEST-001-Product-Commission-Structure` |
| Commission rule edit | `@commission-rule-edit` | `@TEST-001-Product-Commission-Rule` |
| Agency dashboard global filters | `@global-filters` | `@TEST-001-Agency-Dashboard-Global-Filters` |
| Ops manager dashboard viewing period | `@viewing-period` | `@TEST-001-dashboard-viewing-period` |
| User management | `@user-management` | `@TEST-001-User-Page` |
| Smoke | `@smoke` | `@TEST-001-smoke` |

Derive `{Module}-{Area}` from the page or flow under test (PascalCase or kebab-case slug after `TEST-{NNN}-`). Number each **Module-Area** group independently starting at `001`.

## Rules

1. **One ID per scenario** — assign to `Scenario` and `Scenario Outline` only, not to individual `Examples` rows.
2. **Sequential numbering per Module-Area** — restart at `001` for each `{Module}-{Area}` suffix; never reuse or skip numbers within the same suffix.
3. **Tag placement** — append the ID on the tag line immediately above the scenario, with other tags:

```gherkin
  @product-management @product-create-page @positive @TEST-001-Product-Create-Page
  Scenario: Save product with all valid mandatory fields
```

4. **New scenarios** — use the next available number for that Module-Area suffix (check the highest existing `TEST-NNN-<suffix>` first).
5. **Do not rename existing IDs** unless deliberately renumbering a module; IDs are stable traceability links to manual test cases and reports.

## Checklist when writing or editing features

- [ ] Every scenario has exactly one test case ID tag
- [ ] ID follows `@TEST-{NNN}-{Module}-{Area}` with zero-padded digits
- [ ] Numbers are sequential with no duplicates within each Module-Area suffix
- [ ] Scenario title stays descriptive; the ID lives in tags, not duplicated in the title
- [ ] Scenarios with modals: verify every modal-opening step has a corresponding close step before the scenario ends to leave clean state

## Scenario cleanup

Every `.feature` scenario that opens a modal, popup, or side panel must close it before the scenario ends.

**Why:** Even though the Background may reload the page between scenarios, shared module context means leftover modals can interfere with subsequent scenarios. Explicit cleanup makes intent clear and prevents hidden state leaks.

**Pattern:**

```gherkin
  Scenario: Gross Commission KPI card with breakdown popup
    When I click the Gross Commission card
    Then a "Total Revenue Breakdown" popup is displayed
    And the breakdown popup shows a Category summary table
    And the breakdown popup shows a detail table
    When I close the sidebar modal on agency dashboard
```

Guiding principles:
1. Place the close step as the **last step** in the scenario, after all validation is done.
2. Use a generic step like `When I close the sidebar modal on agency dashboard` (backs a `loc.page.getByTestId(/modal-close/i)` locator) when there is a single close button matching that pattern.
3. Use named close methods (`closeGrossCommissionModal()`) when the scenario must close a specific modal by name.
